agent-ops task task-0c5ae242-54e1-4cfb-8a9c-d4d7773cdc2e: Office batch 1: acceptance criteria panel
intent: Batch 1 of the Office redesign. collect.ts taskView already loads each criterion and its newest evidence but collapses them to {verify, review, passed, total}. Pass per-criterion rows (id, description, status PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN or null when unverified, finishedAt, failureClass, exitCode) plus the task title through the snapshot lobby desks and sceneModel floors. In room mode the right column (#work-panel) switches from the global work list to the room panel: criteria list, open questions, commands; overview keeps the work list. Task text is rendered with textContent only. No new files are read; run-state workers keep counts only (no criteria) in this batch.
criteria:
- snapshot-criteria: Office snapshot lobby desks carry per-criterion rows (id, description, status PASS/FAIL/UNKNOWN or null, finishedAt, failureClass, exitCode) and the task title for the attached task, taken from the newest evidence per verifier/phase; desks without a task carry no rows. Covered by tests/office/collect.test.ts or snapshot.test.ts.
- criteria-consistent: For every desk, the number of criterion rows with status PASS equals progress.passed and the row count equals progress.total, so the panel and the n/m summary cannot disagree. Covered by a test with mixed PASS/FAIL/unverified criteria.
- scene-criteria: sceneModel exposes the criteria rows on each floor (empty array when the room has no task or comes from a run). Covered by tests/office/scene.test.ts.
- room-panel: In room mode the right column shows the room panel listing every criterion with its id, description and status text, followed by questions and commands; in overview mode it shows the global work list; task-supplied text is set via textContent, never innerHTML. Covered by tests/office/client.test.ts using the node:vm stub pattern.
